# Scroll Substrate (HUD base architecture)

Decisions of record: `docs/overhaul/EXPERIENCE_DECISIONS.md` (`X#`) and `docs/overhaul/PLATFORM_DECISIONS.md` (`P#`). If this rule and those docs disagree, the docs win; fix the rule in the same PR.

## 1. What is locked (never edit for a feature)

| Base piece | Path | Owns |
|---|---|---|
| `JarvisRoot` | `core/root/` (mounted by `app/layout.tsx`) | QueryClient, L0 backdrop, L1 substrate, portal roots |
| Substrate | `substrate/` | The only WebGL context, orb presets, state modifiers |
| Scroll engine + director | `core/scroll/` | Lenis, snap, scroll progress, auto-scroll rules |
| Sections | `core/sections/` | Registry, `SectionStack`, `SectionFrame`, slots |
| Stores | `core/stores/` | Turn FSM runner, desk, task queue, section state |
| FSM | `lib/orchestratorFsm.ts` | Pure reducer + `effectsFor` — no DOM, no scroll, no fetch |

Features live in `features/<id>/`, import **only** from `@/sdk` (+ React Bits, `motion/react`, third-party libs), and register with **one line** in `features/index.ts`. ESLint `no-restricted-imports` enforces this.

## 2. Substrate hoisting

```text
app/layout.tsx (server)
└─ <JarvisRoot> (client)            mounted once — survives every route change
   ├─ <Backdrop/>        L0  fixed
   ├─ <SubstrateHost/>   L1  fixed, pointer-events:none, one <canvas> → worker OffscreenCanvas
   ├─ {children}         L2  page content (route)
   ├─ #jarvis-foreground L3  portal root (decor + chrome)
   ├─ #jarvis-modal          portal root
   └─ #jarvis-toast          portal root
app/page.tsx  → <Landing/> + <SectionStack/>   (Lenis lives here, not in the root)
```

- One canvas, one context, created inside `useEffect`, disposed in cleanup (StrictMode-safe). Never `transferControlToOffscreen` twice on one element.
- Off `/`: post `{ type: "route", active: false }` → engine freezes and hides. Never dispose on navigation.
- Context loss is handled inside `SubstrateEngine` (debounced rebuild). UI must keep working when `window.__JARVIS_SUBSTRATE__.contextLost` is true.
- No other component may call `getContext("webgl"|"webgl2")` on `/`. React Bits WebGL bits (`Particles`, `LightRays`, `EvilEye`) are not used on the desk.

## 3. The 4-tier layer system

Use the Tailwind tokens only — **never a raw `z-index`**.

| Token | z | Tier | Rules |
|---|---|---|---|
| `z-backdrop` | 0 | L0 | CSS/SVG only. Parallax `translateY(-0.3·scrollY)` via `useTransform`. |
| `z-substrate` | 10 | L1 | Canvas only. Motion comes from uniforms, never CSS transforms. |
| `z-content` | 20 | L2 | Sections (`100dvh` each) and cards. Scrolls 1×. |
| `z-decor` | 30 | L3 | Decorative SVG/CSS, `pointer-events:none`, 1.2–1.4× speed, ≤0.35 opacity over cards, ≤4 per section, static on reduced motion. |
| `z-chrome` | 40 | L3 | StatusCluster, SectionNav, TaskDock, CommandBaton. Fixed. |
| `z-modal` | 50 | — | HITL, compose, prefs, Google connect (portal `#jarvis-modal`). |
| `z-toast` | 60 | — | Toasts. |
| `z-landing` | 70 | — | Landing overlay only. |

Section content boxes subtract `--chrome-top`, `--chrome-bottom`, `--nav-w`, `--dock-w`, so cards never sit under chrome.

## 4. Scroll rules

- Document scroll, driven by Lenis from motion's frame loop (`frame.update`); snap = Lenis snap to section tops (never CSS `scroll-snap`).
- Scroll position is read from `sectionStore` (`progress` in section units, `active` section) — never from `window.scrollY` or scroll/wheel listeners in features.
- Any inner scroll area: `data-lenis-prevent` + `overscroll-contain`. Wheel-owning widgets (drawing viewer zoom) must also `data-lenis-prevent`.
- Programmatic scroll only via the director: `useSection().go(id)` (user) or FSM `scroll` effects (auto). Never `window.scrollTo` / `element.scrollIntoView`.
- Auto scroll is dropped when pinned, when the user interacted in the last 1200 ms, or when a modal is open. Reduced motion → instant jump.

## 5. Orb pipeline (scroll + FSM → uniforms)

```text
useScroll → useTransform(pos) → useMotionValueEvent → blendPresets(sections, pos)
  → (≤1 post / frame, only if changed) → worker {type:"orb", target}
turnStore effect "orb-mode" → {type:"mode", mode}      voice.ts analyser → {type:"level", value}
SubstrateEngine: springs(target) × stateModifier(mode, level) → uCenter uScale uAccent uDim uSpread uSwirl uTint uState uLevel
```

- Presets are data in `substrate/presets.ts`; a section declares its `orb` preset. Tune numbers there, never in the shader.
- State modifiers change **shape/brightness/tint only**. The **only** positional override is `hitl` while the modal is open (centre, scale ≥ 0.6). Parked approvals do not move the orb.
- Features influence the orb only through `useOrb().glance()` / `.pulse()`.

## 6. Template — add a card (most common)

```ts
// features/toolwear/feature.ts
import { defineFeature, defineCard } from "@/sdk";
import { lazy } from "react";

export default defineFeature({
  id: "toolwear",
  title: "Tool wear",
  cards: [
    defineCard({
      id: "toolwear.recent",
      slot: "monitor.rail",          // monitor.main | monitor.rail | casual.left | casual.right | engineering.side | engineering.deck-empty
      order: 40,
      size: "md",
      component: lazy(() => import("./RecentInsertsCard")),
    }),
  ],
});
```

```tsx
// features/toolwear/RecentInsertsCard.tsx
"use client";
import { useFeatureQuery, api } from "@/sdk";

export default function RecentInsertsCard() {
  const q = useFeatureQuery(["toolwear", "recent"], () => api.get("/api/toolwear/recent"), {
    topics: ["toolwear"],
  });
  if (!q.data) return null;             // FeatureBoundary shows the skeleton / failure tile
  return <ul data-lenis-prevent className="max-h-full overflow-y-auto overscroll-contain">…</ul>;
}
```

Then add `toolwear` to `features/index.ts`. Nothing else in `core/` changes.

## 7. Template — add a full-screen section

```ts
defineSection({
  id: "shopfloor",
  order: 250,                           // between Casual (200) and Engineering (300); must be unique
  label: "Shop floor",
  icon: "factory",
  workspace: undefined,                 // only the 3 core sections map to HudWorkspace
  orb: { center: [0.9, 0.2], scale: 0.2, accent: "#9ad0ff", dim: 0.4, spread: 0.3, swirl: 0.5 },
  theme: { bg: "oklch(11% 0.01 240)" /* … ThemeTokens */ },
  decor: [{ kind: "ticks", edge: "right", speed: 1.3 }],
  lazy: { mountWithin: 1, unmountBeyond: 2 },
  slots: ["shopfloor.main"],
  component: lazy(() => import("./ShopFloorSection")),
});
```

The section gets nav entry, snap point, orb blend, backdrop tint, lazy mount and error boundary automatically. The component renders a layout that places its `<Slot id="shopfloor.main"/>`; it must fill `100dvh` minus chrome and never scroll the page.

## 8. Template — add an approval kind

Backend (`features/<id>/approvals.py`): `ApprovalKind(kind, summarize, execute)`. Frontend: `defineApprovalView({ kind, Card, Chip })`. The core envelope (claim-once, Idempotency-Key, `external_effects` bracket, copy discipline) is automatic and **not overridable**. Authorize/Reject happen only in the full modal, never from a chip.

## 9. Template — voice command, Hermes tool, job (backend)

```py
FEATURE = Feature(
    id="toolwear",
    router=router,                                           # APIRouter(prefix="/api/toolwear")
    intents=[Intent(id="toolwear.show", route="ui_command", section="monitor",
                    examples=["show tool wear", "which inserts changed today", …])],
    tools=[ToolSpec(name="log_insert", description=…, params_schema=…, fn=log_insert)],   # → jarvis_toolwear_log_insert
    jobs=[Job(id="toolwear.rollup", every_s=900, fn=rollup)],
    topics=["toolwear"],
)
```

Tools with `external=True` may only queue a pending action. Jobs publish a topic so cards refetch.

## 10. Hard don'ts (review blockers)

- Editing `core/`, `substrate/`, `orchestratorFsm.ts` or `app/layout.tsx` to ship a feature.
- A second WebGL context, a `requestAnimationFrame` loop, or a `scroll`/`wheel` listener in feature code.
- Raw `z-index`, `position: fixed` outside L3 chrome, or content taller than its section without an inner scroll area.
- Conditional hooks around lazy sections, `Date.now()`/`localStorage` reads during render (hydration mismatch).
- Showing a number (price, rate, dimension, total) that no tool or master-data row produced.
- Treating a parked approval as authorized.

## 11. Merge checklist for any feature

- [ ] Registered in `features/index.ts` (and `backend/app/features/__init__.py` if it has backend parts)
- [ ] Only `@/sdk` imports from Jarvis code; `npm run lint` clean
- [ ] `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test`, pytest green; `npm run api:types` re-run if routes changed
- [ ] Reduced-motion path checked; inner scroll areas carry `data-lenis-prevent`
- [ ] Failure tile verified (throw once in dev) and no layout shift
- [ ] Headless load of `/` shows exactly one WebGL context (`--enable-unsafe-swiftshader`)
